※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4022 LANG_TAKE_RUN_HAS_A_STEP

※ What `†l⟦i…j⟧` takes out is one piece, and what followed it moves down by the
※ length of the piece.  Every other element of a run would leave the rest in
※ pieces, each moved by a different distance -- which is a filter over the list
※ and not a run taken out of it, so a step is refused here though a slice may
※ have one.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let l: mut [u8] = [1u8, 2u8, 3u8, 4u8]
    †l⟦0…4…2⟧
    0u6
